para('NovaPunk LLC | Company website architecture and implementation reference')
para('Author: Sungwon Son | Version: 1.0 | Issue date: 4 November 2026 | Local project: C:/dev/homepage | Classification: Internal technical reference')
para('I built the NovaPunk company website as a statically exported Next.js application, supported by standalone HTML service demonstrations and recorded project media. GitHub Actions builds the production files and deploys them to Firebase Hosting through Workload Identity Federation. Production delivery does not require a continuously running Node.js application server. This document describes the inspected implementation, deployment identity, content workflow and operational boundaries so that I can maintain the site and explain the engineering decisions.')
para('Evidence baseline: local source and configuration inspected on 4 November 2026; Git working tree was clean before this document was generated, and the latest local commit was 6e70426 Diagnose Firebase project access. Historical deployment success and domain availability were confirmed in the earlier project conversation. No live cloud login, DNS lookup, remote IAM audit, production build or browser test was performed for this documentation task. Package versions below are the resolved versions in package-lock.json.')
h('1 Purpose and Scope')
para('The site presents NovaPunk LLC, explains five business services, shows selected engineering examples, and provides an email inquiry channel. World Model based AI is the company positioning. The first service is Custom AI Agents and receives a full width card; the remaining four cards form two pairs at medium and larger widths. On smaller screens, the same content is stacked.')
para('This website is the presentation layer for the business. The models, agents, warehouse pipelines and simulators described on the demonstration pages do not execute inside the website. They are represented by research narratives, figures, architecture explanations and prerecorded videos. NovaNutri development and AWS experimentation are separate projects, not hidden runtime dependencies of this website.')
h('2 Architecture Overview')
code('AUTHORING AND RELEASE\nWindows VS Code\n  Next.js pages + shared TypeScript configuration\n  JSON demo content -> optional Python HTML generator\n             |\n        Git commit and push to main\n             |\nGitHub Actions: npm ci -> next build -> out artifact\n             |\nGitHub OIDC -> GCP WIF provider -> service account\n             |\nFirebase CLI -> Firebase Hosting release\n\nVISITOR REQUEST\nBrowser -> Namecheap DNS for novapunkai.com\n        -> Firebase Hosting HTTPS delivery\n        -> exported HTML, CSS, JS, images and MP4\n        -> browser interaction / email client via mailto')
