para('ServiceOverview reads the shared services array and uses md:col-span-2 for Custom AI Agents. The first four service cards link to /demos/custom-ai-agents.html, /demos/physics-world-models.html, /demos/business-world-models.html and /demos/cloud-data-ai.html. Demo links disable Next.js prefetch. The website development card is an article containing the implementation example instead of a demo link.')
para('content/service-demos.json is the source for the four detailed static pages. scripts/generate-service-demos.py reads it, escapes inserted text and writes public/demos/*.html. The generator renders problems, deliverables, architecture and automation flow content where provided, figures, scope, reported metrics, limitations and source links. It marks the examples as internal research or prototypes and states that no live agent, simulator or model runs on the page. Reported project metrics are not independently rerun by the website.')
para('The generator is an authoring tool rather than a production service or CI prerequisite. Generated HTML is committed to Git, so editing JSON alone is insufficient: regenerate the intended pages and commit the resulting HTML. The main TypeScript service summaries and JSON detail pages are separate content sources and need editorial consistency checks.')
para('The harvest video directory contains dyn_compare_tree23_v3.mp4, pick_one_annotated.mp4, pick_two_annotated.mp4 and plan_tree23_gripper_v34.mp4. A separate public/videos/videos.mp4 template asset also exists; its presence does not demonstrate that it is used by an active route. The final gripper simulation was added as a recorded example rather than live browser computation.')
h('6 Styling Branding and Metadata')
para('The global stylesheet imports Tailwind CSS, Preline variants, Swiper styling and local configuration, general and Swiper CSS. Tailwind forms and typography plugins are registered. Geist and Roboto are declared through next/font/google using CSS variables for body and heading text. The build may require network access to obtain fonts on an uncached machine; the current implementation is not a guaranteed offline build.')
para('Navbar imports src/assets/images/logo-light.svg and renders it with NovaPunk LLC alternative text. Static demonstrations use public brand files. The source also retains cosmic logo imagery in PNG and WebP formats. The logo concept was mine and AI assisted generation was part of development history; this technical document does not make a legal originality or copyright guarantee.')
para('The root layout defines title templates, description, keywords, author, favicon, English language and index/follow metadata. Page level metadata supplies route titles and, for About, an additional description. Accessible navigation labels, active page indication and mobile menu state are present in the inspected code. A complete accessibility, SEO or production performance audit was not performed for this document.')
h('7 Static Build and Local Execution')
code('cd C:\\dev\\homepage\nnpm.cmd ci\nnpm.cmd run dev\n# Development preview: http://localhost:3000\n\n# Production static export, default output\nnpm.cmd run build\nnpm.cmd run preview\n# Static preview: http://localhost:4173')
para('next.config.ts sets output to export, trailingSlash to true and images.unoptimized to true. Under the default build configuration, out contains deployable static files. Routes map to directory index.html files, public assets are copied, and the Next.js server image optimizer is not required. No server-side request rendering, server actions or API route backend is implemented in the current site.')
para('The configuration allows NOVAPUNK_BUILD_DIR to override distDir. The project deployment note records a local .next-build export workflow while Next.js still uses .next intermediates in this version. Treat this as the documented project-specific behavior; use the default out build to match CI, and verify the chosen output exists before preview or deployment. Do not assume that the custom export path provides fully isolated development/build caches.')
para('scripts/serve-static.mjs serves out by default and can accept another directory argument. It binds to 127.0.0.1:4173, supports GET and HEAD, resolves directory index files, checks path containment, sets MIME types and supports one explicit byte range for MP4 seeking. It redirects waitlist to Contact. This is a local preview utility, not the production hosting process.')
h('8 Continuous Integration and Deployment')
para('Source repository: https://github.com/isupernova-io/novapunk-homepage . Release branch: main. Workflow: .github/workflows/firebase-hosting.yml . Pushes to main, pull requests and workflow_dispatch can start the workflow. The concurrency group is hosting-${github.ref}; newer runs can cancel an earlier run in the same group.')
para('The build job runs on ubuntu-latest, checks out source, installs Node.js 22, uses npm ci with package-lock.json, and runs npm run build. It uploads out as hosting-output with hidden files included. The deploy job downloads this artifact instead of rebuilding it. It installs Firebase CLI 15.33.0, authenticates, checks access to the target Firebase project and deploys Hosting. The current workflow does not run an explicit lint or browser test step.')
matrix(['Repository variable','Configured value or purpose'],[['FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID','novapunk-homepage-a8912'],['FIREBASE_DEPLOY_ENABLED','true enables deployment when the other conditions pass']])
para('Deployment requires main, an event other than pull_request, the enabled flag and a nonempty project ID. A pull request is therefore a build check, not a configured Firebase preview-channel deployment. The default token permission is contents:read; the deploy job adds id-token:write for GitHub OIDC.')
code('npm ci -> npm run build -> upload out\n       -> download out -> OIDC authentication\n       -> Firebase Management API access check\n       -> firebase deploy --only hosting --project "$FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID" --non-interactive')
