para('The organization policy iam.disableServiceAccountKeyCreation blocked the original JSON key approach. I used GitHub OIDC and WIF instead of disabling that policy. google-github-actions/auth@v3 requests an access token and prepares Application Default Credentials. No long lived service-account private key or FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT secret is required by this workflow. Credentials belong to CI; no deploy key is embedded in browser JavaScript.')
para('Deployment originally failed because the Firebase Management API and later Firebase Hosting API were disabled in consumer project 1078070273018. After activating firebase.googleapis.com and firebasehosting.googleapis.com there, deployment succeeded in the recorded Actions run. The project access check now calls Firebase Management API before deployment to expose API and IAM failures separately. An access error does not justify substituting the identity project for the target project.')
h('10 Hosting DNS and Cache Behavior')
para('Firebase Hosting serves out and ignores firebase.json, dot paths and node_modules. It issues a 301 redirect for /waitlist and descendants to /contact/. _next/static assets receive public,max-age=31536000,immutable; MP4 files receive public,max-age=3600. The configuration does not add a universal SPA rewrite, because exported routes are real static pages.')
