para('During setup, stale routing to the old IP caused ACME challenge failure and a certificate name warning. The domain was subsequently reported working. DNS and certificate status were not checked again for this issue of the document. The record does not establish www subdomain configuration. Browser cache clearing was reported during initial access troubleshooting, but routine visitors should not depend on clearing all browser history to use a release.')
para('Hashed Next.js assets suit the long immutable policy. Public videos use stable names and a one hour cache; replacing the bytes at the same URL can delay visible changes for cached visitors. Versioned filenames are an option for later media updates. No automated cache or media versioning change was made for this documentation task.')
h('11 Content Editing and Release Procedure')
para('For shared service copy, edit src/config/services.ts. For navigation, edit src/config/navigation.ts. For page content, edit the relevant src/app route. For demonstration detail content, edit content/service-demos.json and regenerate public/demos HTML with the Python authoring script from the repository root. Verify actual generated differences before committing; do not regenerate unrelated material unnecessarily.')
code('python scripts/generate-service-demos.py\n# Uses an existing local Python installation with the standard library.\n\nnpm.cmd run build\nnpm.cmd run preview\ngit status\ngit add <reviewed changed files>\ngit commit -m "Describe the website change"\ngit push origin main')
para('The commands are a maintenance reference and were not executed as a release in this task. After push, inspect both build and deploy jobs in GitHub Actions. Check the Firebase release and then the relevant public routes, demo images and videos. A successful Git push alone is not proof of production deployment. Preserve the deployment commit and release record to support diagnosis or a planned rollback.')
para('When a release needs reversal, first identify the last known good source and Hosting release. A reviewed revert commit followed by the normal pipeline is one source-controlled recovery path. A Hosting rollback, if used through the console, must be reconciled with repository history. No rollback was executed or independently tested for this document.')
