para('If content editing through an administration interface is needed, CMS integration requires an explicit architecture change involving runtime hosting, persistence and access control. If an inquiry API or live AI demonstration is added, it needs a backend endpoint, server-side credentials, validation, cost controls and observability. These are future engineering tasks, not capabilities supplied automatically by static hosting. No CMS, database or API service was added while writing this document.')
h('13 Operational Findings and Maintenance Priorities')
para('Keep the actual Firebase project ID distinct from the display name and the identity project. Keep provider conditions, service-account impersonation and target project roles documented together. If deployment fails, read the access check HTTP response and the consumer project named in the error before changing permissions. Do not restore service-account private keys merely to bypass a disabled-key policy.')
para('The Actions screenshot in the project record reported successful build and deploy, alongside warnings about Node 20 based action runtimes and the ubuntu-latest image transition. The source still uses v4 checkout/setup-node/artifact actions and ubuntu-latest. Node.js 22 for npm build and the JavaScript runtime used internally by an action are separate settings. Action upgrades and runner selection should be reviewed in a later tested change; they have not been silently modified for this document.')
para('Other maintenance candidates are removing unused template components, aligning generated and React navigation, adding explicit lint and smoke checks to CI, confirming domain canonicalization and www requirements, measuring video payload performance, and clarifying the Projects publication plan. These observations are implementation follow-ups, not reasons to describe the inspected site as having those improvements already.')
